<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo April oil imports slump, gas imports soar.</title>
<headline>Yugo April oil imports slump, gas imports soar.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL IMPORTS	    APRIL     MARCH     APRIL 96</p>
<p> In tonnes		     69,762    192,389     16,181</p>
<p> In million USD		    11	   35	    3</p>
<p>OIL DERIVATIVES IMPORTS</p>
<p> In tonnes			4,763     17,531     87,296</p>
<p> In million USD		     3	    5	   18</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS IMPORTS</p>
<p> In tonnes		    150,968     26,651	   --</p>
<p> In million USD		    21	    4	   --</p>
<p>NOTES -- Cumulative January-April crude oil imports stood at 764,959 tonnes and were worth a total of $136 million.</p>
<p>Cumulative oil derivatives imports for the first four months amounted to 169,481 tonnes and totalled $46 million.</p>
<p>Cumulative natural gas imports for the same period stood at 252,141 tonnes and were worth $35 million. -- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
